@startuml
title MyNetMate - Authentication / Audit component assembly\nbackend feature/11-audit-writer @ b862c60 | application-owned contracts
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 55
skinparam padding 10
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #F7FBFF
skinparam componentBorderColor #315A78
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFBEA
component "Authentication / Audit (selected internal structure)" as AuthSystem {
 component "auth : AuthenticationService" as Auth {
  portout " " as R_A01
  portout " " as R_A04
  portin " " as P_A07
 }
 component "bootstrap : UserProvisioning" as Bootstrap {
  portout " " as R_A02
  portout " " as R_A05
 }
 component "adapter : AuthAuditAdapterModule" as Adapter {
  portout " " as R_A03
  portin " " as P_A01
  portin " " as P_A02
 }
 component "writer : AuditAppendModule" as Writer {
  portin " " as P_A03
 }
 component "reader : AuditReadModule" as Reader {
  portout " " as R_A06
  portout " " as R_A07
 }
 component "database : DatabaseRuntime" as Database {
  portin " " as P_A04
  portin " " as P_A05
  portin " " as P_A06
 }
 R_A01 -(0- P_A01 : A01: IRecordAuthEvent
 R_A02 -(0- P_A02 : A02: IRecordAuthEvent
 R_A03 -(0- P_A03 : A03: AuditWriter
 R_A04 -(0- P_A04 : A04: IAsyncSessionFactory
 R_A05 -(0- P_A05 : A05: IAsyncSessionFactory
 R_A06 -(0- P_A06 : A06: IAsyncSessionFactory
 R_A07 -(0- P_A07 : A07: IAuthorize
}
legend bottom left
 Square = UML Port (name suppressed). Socket = required; ball = provided.
 Each assembly joins two simple ports for ONE named interface.
 role : ComponentType denotes a part; types are logical software-module abstractions.
 Contract IDs map to operations and immutable source evidence in README / CONTRACTS.md.
 Writer receives the caller-owned db session in AuditWriter; it does NOT call a session factory.
 The writer adds and flushes an AuditLog; the caller owns commit / rollback.
 HTTP routers and permission-boundary internals are omitted; see the separate web-contract view.
endlegend
@enduml
